    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.24.0</title>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:11:34 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22400</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.24.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Ponds come from one list: no duplicate or folder-name ponds. The sidebar, a pond's home and its settings all read the same directory, in its order.</li><li>Shared ponds work like your own: their threads sit in the sidebar with the starter's avatar, open in the normal workbench, show a read-only Changes view, and "Run on &lt;owner&gt;'s Mac" starts a thread there. Controls follow your role; what only the starter can do is greyed out and says who can.</li><li>Names come from your Squeak sign-in, never typed. Joining a pond needs you signed in.</li><li>Threads with more than one person read like a group chat, with each person's avatar beside their messages.</li><li>Short invite codes: a 6-character code (K7P-4QD) that lasts 10 minutes and works once, with three matching words on both screens. The long link stays for longer sharing.</li><li>Every thread can be archived, not only Squeak chats: right-click, or Chat › Archive Thread (⇧⌘A). Conductor, terminal and Codex threads are hidden in Squeak only; a thread someone else started is hidden from your view only.</li><li>An Archived entry sits at the foot of the sidebar and opens a page of every archived thread, by pond, newest first, with search, Open and Unarchive.</li><li>⌘T always opens a new chat tab (⌃⇧` opens a terminal tab); closing the terminal puts you back in the composer; every divider is one thin line that brightens on hover.</li><li>"Copy web link" and the QR code point to the new web app at squeak.onslate.in.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.39</h4><ul><li>Main: every git pond has a Main place, its own folder. ⌘N starts a thread there; "In: Main ▾" picks a stream instead, and if Main is busy you're offered a new stream.</li><li>New streams clone dependencies (node_modules, .venv, ignored .env files) from the pond with copy-on-write, so they take almost no extra disk.</li><li>Ponds shared with you carry the sharer's initials on their icon; the sidebar filter has Mine and Shared with me.</li><li>The pond dashboard no longer jumps: its status lives in one fixed line in the header, and an idle shared pond talks to the cloud far less.</li><li>Every update action (Install, Restart to update, Cancel, Try again) is quiet text, in the sidebar, the menu-bar panel and Settings.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.38</h4><ul><li>Chat tabs fit their name: the close button sits right after the title instead of at the far edge.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
